Subject: intr_attach and intr_detach: the level-2 and level-6 chains

The stock level-2 autovector (p2int) calls every entry of int2_tbl with
a pointer to a zeroed longword and ignores what they return; the level-6
one (p6int) calls aciabintr, the CIA-B handler, alone.  The core now
adds a chain to each without moving a stock handler: dlm_intr_init()
(from dlm_init) puts dlm_int2_walk in int2_tbl's last handler slot,
which calls the handler it displaced first and then the attached ones;
the kernel build weakens aciabintr and keeps its body as
__amix_aciabintr, and the core's aciabintr calls it and then the level-6
chain (p6int is its only caller in both Amix kernels).
intr_attach(level, fn, arg, name) and intr_detach(level, fn, arg) are
DDI v1 (amix-dlm docs/contracts/C3-2-symbols-and-ddi.md); a handler is
fn(arg), returns nonzero if its board interrupted, and is always called,
like the stock ones; the claims are counted.  The chains change at IPL 7,
since the DDI spl7 stops at level 4.  30-module-core.md section 4 (patch
10 in section 2).

